      "stop_reason": "end_turn",
      "tool_uses": [],
      "assistant_text": "The **Guarded Write Journal** page (from [[write-journal]]) describes a mechanism that provides all-or-nothing write semantics for file operations without requiring a database. Here\u0027s what it covers:\n\n- **Purpose**: Before any file is overwritten, the guarded tool executor first records that file\u0027s prior state in an in-memory write journal \u2014 either its previous content (if it existed) or a record that it didn\u0027t exist.\n\n- **Rollback on failure**: If an agent run fails \u2014 whether due to exceeding a turn cap, an unrecoverable error, or denied write attempts \u2014 the journal can reverse all recorded writes in reverse order: restoring prior content for files that existed before, and deleting any newly created files.\n\n- **All-or-nothing semantics**: This gives each run transactional semantics without needing a database transaction; the in-memory journal itself serves as the transaction log for the duration of that single run.\n\n- **Query agent behavior**: The Query agent (which is what we\u0027re currently running) doesn\u0027t use the journal\u0027s rollback path since it has no write capability at all \u2014 the journal infrastructure exists in the shared runtime library but is only populated by agents that actually write files.",
